# Story 1: What Is Rysh? (60s)
# Hook: A terminal that thinks. Shell mode runs commands. Prompt mode talks to AI.
# Duration: 60s
# Source: story-01-what-is-rysh.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 9

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
A terminal that thinks. Shell mode runs commands. Prompt mode talks to AI.

[00:03.0 --> 00:07.0]
Start rysh and you land in shell mode -- your familiar terminal.

[00:07.0 --> 00:13.0]
In shell mode, everything works like a normal terminal. Run any command you want.

[00:13.0 --> 00:20.0]
Double-press Escape to switch to prompt mode. Watch the prompt change to < -- now you're talking to AI.

[00:20.0 --> 00:32.0]
Ask the AI anything. It sees your terminal context.

[00:32.0 --> 00:37.0]
Press Escape to go back to shell mode.

[00:37.0 --> 00:43.0]
Ctrl+P enters pane mode. Press n to split right -- now you have two independent terminals side by side.

[00:43.0 --> 00:49.0]
Ctrl+T enters tab mode. Press n for a new tab -- a whole separate workspace.

[00:49.0 --> 00:57.0]
Navigate your workspace: brackets switch tabs, Tab key cycles panes. Your AI-powered terminal is ready.

